.TH TRACEBUF 1 "May 13, 2026"
.UC 4
.SH NAME
tracebuf \- display kernel I/O statistics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tracebuf
[\fB\-w secs\fP]
[\fB\-i iter\fP]
[\fB\-h num\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
With no argument
.B tracebuf
prints the kernel \fBtracebuf\fP array once and exits.
.PP
The options are:
.TP 10
\-i iter
Specifies the number of reports.
.TP 10
\-h num
print the header every 
.I num
reports.
.TP 10
\-w secs
wait 
.I secs
seconds between reports.
.PP
Each report:
.TP 15
breadhit
buffer read found in cache
.TP 15
breadmiss
buffer read not in cache
.TP 15
breadhitra
buffer read-ahead found in cache
.TP 15
breadmissra
buffer read-ahead not in cache
.TP 15
brelese
buffer released with no I/O implied
.TP 15
swapio
swap I/o request
.TP 15
bhit
read cache rate [breadhit/(breadhit+breadmiss)]
.SH FILES
/dev/kmem
.br
/unix
.SH HISTORY
.B tracebuf
appeared in 2.11BSD 35th Anniversary Edition
